t value into a data path, then persists through the normal autosave path. Requires a non-empty path and an object value. Unknown fileKey warns once, then falls back to homeConfig."},"6075":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-223","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"Config.remove(dataPath, fileKey)"},"6076":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-224","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"Deletes a nested property and autosaves. Returns false and changes nothing when the path does not exist. Unknown fileKey warns once, then falls back to homeConfig."},"6077":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-225","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"Example"},"6078":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-226","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"Result"},"6079":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-227","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"Config.set(\"notifications.isDnd\", true)"},"6080":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-228","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"true and document changed plus autosave write queued; true with no write/revision when already equal; false on empty path or undefined value"},"6081":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-229","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"Config.set(\"wifi.enabled\", false, \"networkConfig\")"},"6082":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-230","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"true and networkConfig document changed plus autosave write queued (homeConfig when key is unknown); false when rejected"},"6083":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-231","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"Config.update(\"notifications\", {\"isDnd\": true})"},"6084":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-232","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"true and value deep-merged plus autosave write queued; false when path is empty or value is not an object"},"6085":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-233","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"Config.update(\"wifi\", {\"enabled\": true}, \"networkConfig\")"},"6086":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-234","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"true and networkConfig value deep-merged plus autosave write queued; false when rejected"},"6087":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-235","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"Config.remove(\"notifications.isDnd\")"},"6088":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-236","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"true and property deleted plus autosave write queued; false when the path does not exist"},"6089":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-237","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"Config.remove(\"wifi.enabled\", \"networkConfig\")"},"6090":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-238","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"true and property deleted from networkConfig plus autosave write queued; false when the path does not exist"},"6091":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-239","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Model: autosave everything + explicit checkpoint. Every set()/update()/remove()/undo()/redo()/revert() updates memory and immediately queues a disk write. isDirty means \"document differs from the last save()/load baseline\", not \"disk differs\" — after autosave the file already matches memory, but the file stays dirty until save() establishes a new baseline and wipes history."},"6092":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-240","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Each mutation records one compact forward-delta entry (past), up to historyLimit (100) entries for past + future combined. When over the limit the oldest past entry is discarded first so redo is preserved. A new mutation clears future (kills redo). save() and revert() wipe both stacks."},"6093":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-241","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"How to call"},"6094":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-242","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"What does it do"},"6095":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-243","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Config.undo(fileKey)"},"6096":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-244","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Moves the newest past entry to future, restores its before-values, autosaves. Returns false when past is empty or the file is not ready. A no-op undo (entry resolves to the current document) still advances the stack but skips write/revision. Any undo cancels a pending save() checkpoint. Defaults to homeConfig."},"6097":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-245","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Config.redo(fileKey)"},"6098":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-246","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Moves the newest future entry back to past, restores its after-values, autosaves. Returns false when future is empty or the file is not ready. No-op redos advance the stack without write/revision. A new set()/update()/remove() clears future. Defaults to homeConfig."},"6099":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-247","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Config.revert(fileKey)"},"6100":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-248","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Logically while (canUndo) undo(): replays every past before-value in reverse to restore the clean baseline, coalesced into a single document commit (single write, single revision, single documentChanged). Then wipes past + future. Returns false when not ready, or when past is empty and already clean. Undone-to-clean with redo available wipes without disk IO. Defaults to homeConfig."},"6101":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-249","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Config.save(fileKey)"},"6102":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-250","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"True checkpoint. Fails (false) when not ready. Clean + empty history: true no-op, no IO. Clean with leftover history (e.g. undo-to-clean leaves redo): wipes history, true, no IO, no revision. Dirty + write pipeline active: marks checkpoint-when-idle and ensures the newest state is queued; baseline/history reset in onSaved. Dirty + idle + last write failed: forces a rewrite, checkpoint on onSaved. Dirty + idle + disk already matches (normal autosave case): sets baseline + wipes history synchronously, true, no IO (avoids a same-content write that would never complete)."},"6103":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-251","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"IPC"},"6104":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-252","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Result"},"6105":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-253","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"qs ipc call n0ctos-config undo / redo / revert"},"6106":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-254","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"\"true\" on success; \"false\" when there is nothing to undo/redo, when revert is already clean, or when the file is not ready"},"6107":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-255","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"qs ipc call n0ctos-config undoAt networkConfig (same redoAt, revertAt)"},"6108":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-256","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Per-file variants"},"6109":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-257","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"How to call"},"6110":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-258","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"What does it do"},"6111":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-259","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"Config.save(fileKey)"},"6112":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-260","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"True checkpoint (see Undo history). Defaults to homeConfig. Normal set()/update()/remove() already autosave; save() only moves the baseline and wipes history."},"6