 not increment the revision or start a write. A no-op undo()/redo() still advances the history stack but skips revision/signal/write."},"6545":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-693","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#616-read-path-resolution","content":"A path such as:"},"6546":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-694","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#616-read-path-resolution","content":"is split into:"},"6547":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-695","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#616-read-path-resolution","content":"The store walks the selected document:"},"6548":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-696","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#616-read-path-resolution","content":"If any part does not exist, the fallback value is returned."},"6549":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-697","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#616-read-path-resolution","content":"An empty path also returns the fallback."},"6550":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-698","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#616-read-path-resolution","content":"has() implements existence by reading with a unique sentinel object:"},"6551":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-699","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#617-write-path-resolution","content":"For:"},"6552":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-700","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#617-write-path-resolution","content":"the store clones the current document and walks to:"},"6553":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-701","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#617-write-path-resolution","content":"Missing or invalid intermediate objects are replaced with objects. The final property becomes:"},"6554":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-702","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#617-write-path-resolution","content":"The complete updated document is then replaced into the store."},"6555":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-703","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#617-write-path-resolution","content":"Null, non-object, and array intermediates are replaced. Values are cloned so later caller-side mutation cannot affect stored state."},"6556":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-704","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#618-why-documents-are-cloned","content":"The store avoids directly mutating nested members of the public reactive document."},"6557":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-705","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#618-why-documents-are-cloned","content":"Instead:"},"6558":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-706","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#618-why-documents-are-cloned","content":"This makes the reactive state transition explicit and prevents consumers from holding references that change without a document replacement."},"6559":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-707","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#618-why-documents-are-cloned","content":"Returned documents are snapshot clones: documentFor()/getDocument return a deep copy, so mutating the result never affects the store. set() inputs and internal merge results are likewise cloned. IPC results are serialized with JSON.stringify() rather than exposing live objects."},"6560":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-708","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#619-deep-merge","content":"update() uses a recursive object merge."},"6561":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-709","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#619-deep-merge","content":"Current:"},"6562":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-710","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#619-deep-merge","content":"Patch:"},"6563":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-711","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#619-deep-merge","content":"Result:"},"6564":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-712","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#619-deep-merge","content":"Objects merge recursively. Primitive values, arrays, and null replace the previous value."},"6565":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-713","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#620-set-and-update","content":"The relationship is:"},"6566":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-714","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#620-set-and-update","content":"update() eventually uses the normal set() path for persistence:"},"6567":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-715","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#621-write-lifecycle-autosave--checkpoint","content":"A normal configuration write follows:"},"6568":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-716","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#621-write-lifecycle-autosave--checkpoint","content":"Autosave writes never move the baseline. Only an explicit save() checkpoint does:"},"6569":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-717","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#621-write-lifecycle-autosave--checkpoint","content":"set(), update(), remove(), undo(), redo(), and revert() all queue saves through the file's controller. If the controller does not exist yet, the dirty state remains in the store and onObjectAdded() queues the save once the controller appears. Any mutation after save() cancels a pending completeSaveWhenIdle checkpoint."},"6570":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-718","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#622-overlapping-writes","content":"Suppose:"},"6571":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-719","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#622-overlapping-writes","content":"starts a write and then:"},"6572":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-720","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#622-overlapping-writes","content":"happen before the first write finishes."},"6573":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-721","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#622-overlapping-writes","content":"The service keeps only the latest serialized state in:"},"6574":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-722","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#622-overlapping-writes","content":"The lifecycle becomes:"},"6575":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-723","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#622-overlapping-writes","content":"When A completes, the latest state is written."},"6576":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-724","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#623-why-the-latest-state-wins","content":"Configuration represents current state."},"6577":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-725","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#623-why-the-latest-state-wins","content":"Therefore:"},"6578":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-726","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#623-why-the-latest-state-wins","content":"does not require three simultaneous or sequential disk writes when the state can safely be collapsed to:"},"6579":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-727","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#624-directory-creation","content":"Before writing a file, the service ensures its parent directory exists."},"6580":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-728","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#624-directory-creation","content":"Conceptually:"},"6581":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-729","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#624-directory-creation","content":"This runs through a Process (mkdir -p). While the directory is missing, writes stay queued. On failure the write state is cleared, writeFailed is set, the document stays dirty (baseline untouched), and saveError is emitted. A later save() with writeFailed set forces a rewrite instead of a sync checkpoint."},"6582":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-730","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#625-missing-files","content":"A missing homeConfig file is treated as:"},"6583":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-731","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#625-missing-files","content":"and automatically saved, so the default file is created on first run."},"6584":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-732","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#625-missing-files","content":"Other registered files can remain absent until they are explicitly written."},"6585":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-733","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#625-missing-files","content":"A previously loaded file that disappears externally is treated as an undoable external change: the old document becomes a past entry (op: \"externalReload\"), the document becomes {}, the baseline stays where it was (so the file reads dirty), and externalReload is emitted. undo() restores the pre-delete document and autosaves it."},"6586":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-734","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#626-external-reload","content":"A normal external modification follows:"},"6587":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-735","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#626-external-reload","content":"Only changed documents bump the revision and emit documentUpdated."},"6588":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-736","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#626-external-reload","content":"A real external change is recorded as an undoable history entry (op: \"externalReload\"). The baseline does not move, so the file reads dirty and undo() restores the pre-external document (autosaving it back to disk)."},"6589":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-737","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#627-own-writes-versus-external-writes","content":"A watcher can also report changes caused by the service's own atomic write."},"6590":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-738","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#627-own-writes-versus-external-writes","content":"Therefore the service tracks the full write pipeline:"},"6591":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-739","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#627-own-writes-versus-external-writes","content":"While the pipeline is active, watcher events are ignored and debounced reloads are suppressed before calling FileView.reload():"},"6592":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-740","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#627-own-writes-versus-external-writes","content":"is prevented for normal internal writes. Debounced reloads also check writing before calling FileView.reload()."},"6593":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-741","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#628-save-completion","content":"When FileView reports:"},"6594":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-742","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#628-save-completion","content":"the service:"},"6595":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-743","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#628-save-completion","content":"Then it checks:"},"6596":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-744","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#628-save-completion","content":"If another state is queued:"},"6597":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-745","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#628-save-completion","content":"otherwise, only when completeSaveWhenIdle (set by an explicit save() while dirty) is still set — any mutation after save() cancels it:"},"6598":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-746","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#628-save-completion","content":"Autosave writes always stop after clearing the pipeline flags; they never touch baseline/history. A same-content save() therefore never queues a redundant write — it checkpoints synchronously instead (see 6.21), because a same-content FileView.setText may never emit onSaved."},"6599":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-747","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#629-save-failure","content":"If writing fails:"},"6600":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-748","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#629-save-failure","content":"The failed write's stale text is discarded (writeText = \"\", queuedWriteText = \"\"), the pending save checkpoint is cancelled, writeFailed is set, the pipeline flags are cleared, and saveError is emitted. The document and its history stay intact (still dirty), so nothing is lost in memory."},"6601":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-749","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#629-save-failure","content":"The older state being written never overwrites a newer queued state."},"6602":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-750","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#629-save-failure","content":"A later explicit:"},"6603":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-751","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#629-save-failure","content":"serializes the current in-memory document again — with writeFailed set it forces a rewrite instead of a sync checkpoint — and can retry the operation."},"6604":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/config-752","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/se