/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"true and networkConfig value deep-merged plus autosave write queued; false when rejected"},"6939":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-235","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"Config.remove(\"notifications.isDnd\")"},"6940":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-236","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"true and property deleted plus autosave write queued; false when the path does not exist"},"6941":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-237","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"Config.remove(\"wifi.enabled\", \"networkConfig\")"},"6942":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-238","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#writes","content":"true and property deleted from networkConfig plus autosave write queued; false when the path does not exist"},"6943":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-239","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Model: autosave everything + explicit checkpoint. Every set()/update()/remove()/undo()/redo()/revert() updates memory and immediately queues a disk write. isDirty means \"document differs from the last save()/load baseline\", not \"disk differs\" — after autosave the file already matches memory, but the file stays dirty until save() establishes a new baseline and wipes history."},"6944":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-240","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Each mutation records one compact forward-delta entry (past), up to historyLimit (100) entries for past + future combined. When over the limit the oldest past entry is discarded first so redo is preserved. A new mutation clears future (kills redo). save() and revert() wipe both stacks."},"6945":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-241","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"How to call"},"6946":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-242","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"What does it do"},"6947":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-243","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Config.undo(fileKey)"},"6948":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-244","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Moves the newest past entry to future, restores its before-values, autosaves. Returns false when past is empty or the file is not ready. A no-op undo (entry resolves to the current document) still advances the stack but skips write/revision. Any undo cancels a pending save() checkpoint. Defaults to homeConfig."},"6949":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-245","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Config.redo(fileKey)"},"6950":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-246","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Moves the newest future entry back to past, restores its after-values, autosaves. Returns false when future is empty or the file is not ready. No-op redos advance the stack without write/revision. A new set()/update()/remove() clears future. Defaults to homeConfig."},"6951":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-247","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Config.revert(fileKey)"},"6952":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-248","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Logically while (canUndo) undo(): replays every past before-value in reverse to restore the clean baseline, coalesced into a single document commit (single write, single revision, single documentChanged). Then wipes past + future. Returns false when not ready, or when past is empty and already clean. Undone-to-clean with redo available wipes without disk IO. Defaults to homeConfig."},"6953":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-249","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Config.save(fileKey)"},"6954":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-250","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"True checkpoint. Fails (false) when not ready. Clean + empty history: true no-op, no IO. Clean with leftover history (e.g. undo-to-clean leaves redo): wipes history, true, no IO, no revision. Dirty + write pipeline active: marks checkpoint-when-idle and ensures the newest state is queued; baseline/history reset in onSaved. Dirty + idle + last write failed: forces a rewrite, checkpoint on onSaved. Dirty + idle + disk already matches (normal autosave case): sets baseline + wipes history synchronously, true, no IO (avoids a same-content write that would never complete)."},"6955":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-251","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"IPC"},"6956":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-252","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Result"},"6957":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-253","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"qs ipc call n0ctos-config undo / redo / revert"},"6958":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-254","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"\"true\" on success; \"false\" when there is nothing to undo/redo, when revert is already clean, or when the file is not ready"},"6959":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-255","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"qs ipc call n0ctos-config undoAt networkConfig (same redoAt, revertAt)"},"6960":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-256","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#undo-history","content":"Per-file variants"},"6961":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-257","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"How to call"},"6962":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-258","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"What does it do"},"6963":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-259","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"Config.save(fileKey)"},"6964":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-260","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"True checkpoint (see Undo history). Defaults to homeConfig. Normal set()/update()/remove() already autosave; save() only moves the baseline and wipes history."},"6965":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-261","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"Config.reload(fileKey)"},"6966":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-262","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"Explicitly reloads one file from disk. Discards unsaved local state for that file (baseline = disk, history wiped). Defaults to homeConfig. Rejected while the write pipeline is active."},"6967":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-263","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"Config.reloadAll()"},"6968":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-264","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"Reloads every registered file. Skips files currently being written."},"6969":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-265","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"Example"},"6970":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-266","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"Result"},"6971":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-267","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"Config.save()"},"6972":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-268","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"true checkpoint for homeConfig (sync when idle, deferred to onSaved while writes are in flight); false when no controller exists or not ready"},"6973":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-269","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"Config.save(\"networkConfig\")"},"6974":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-270","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"true checkpoint for networkConfig; false when no controller exists or not ready"},"6975":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-271","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"Config.reload()"},"6976":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-272","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"true and homeConfig reloaded (local dirty state discarded); false while writing or when no controller exists"},"6977":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-273","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"Config.reload(\"networkConfig\")"},"6978":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-274","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"true and networkConfig reloaded (local dirty state discarded); false while writing or when no controller exists"},"6979":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-275","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"Config.reloadAll()"},"6980":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-276","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#file-control","content":"true when every file reloaded; false when one or more files were skipped or failed"},"6981":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-277","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"How to call"},"6982":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-278","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"What does it do"},"6983":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-279","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"Config.registerPath(fileKey, fsPath)"},"6984":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-280","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"Registers one logical file key. Same key plus same path is idempotent. Rejects empty keys/paths, same key with a different path, and duplicate physical paths."},"6985":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-281","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"Config.registerPaths(pathTable)"},"6986":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-282","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"Registers multiple files at once. Requires an object. Returns false when one or more entries fail."},"6987":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-283","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"Config.hasPath(fileKey)"},"6988":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-284","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"Registry lookup. Returns true when the key is registered, false otherwise. Does not fall back to homeConfig."},"6989":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-285","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"Config.pathFor(fileKey)"},"6990":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-286","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"Returns the resolved physical path for a key. Unknown keys fall back to the homeConfig path."},"6991":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-287","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"Config.updatePath(fileKey, fsPath)"},"6992":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-288","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"Changes the physical path of an existing non-default key, discards its old document, and loads the new file. Rejects homeConfig, unregistered keys, empty paths, active write pipelines, and duplicate physical paths."},"6993":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-289","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"Config.removePath(fileKey)"},"6994":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config-290","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/config","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/config#path-registry","content":"Removes a non-default key plus its document, state, and watcher. Leaves the physical file untouched. Rejects homeConfig, unregistered keys, and active write pipelines."},"6995":{"id"