ices/configstore#writes","content":"true and document changed plus autosave write queued; true with no write/revision when already equal; false on empty path or undefined value"},"7793":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-237","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"ConfigStore.update(\"notifications\", {\"isDnd\": true})"},"7794":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-238","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"true and value deep-merged plus autosave write queued; false when path is empty or value is not an object"},"7795":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-239","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"ConfigStore.remove(\"notifications.isDnd\")"},"7796":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-240","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"true and property deleted plus autosave write queued; false when the path did not exist"},"7797":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-241","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"There are no setAt / updateAt / removeAt / getAt QML variants on the store itself: the fileKey third (or second) parameter already selects the file. The *At naming exists only on the IPC layer (getAt, setJsonAt, updateJsonAt, removeAt, saveAt, reloadAt, isReadyAt, and so on)."},"7798":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-242","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"Model: autosave everything + explicit checkpoint. Every set()/update()/remove()/undo()/redo()/revert() updates memory and immediately queues a disk write. isDirty means \"document differs from the last save()/load baseline\", not \"disk differs\" — after autosave the file already matches memory, but the file stays dirty until save() establishes a new baseline and wipes history."},"7799":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-243","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"Each mutation records one compact forward-delta entry (past), up to historyLimit (100) entries for past + future combined. When over the limit the oldest past entry is discarded first so redo is preserved. A new mutation clears future (kills redo). save() and revert() wipe both stacks."},"7800":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-244","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"How to call"},"7801":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-245","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"What does it do"},"7802":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-246","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"ConfigStore.undo(fileKey)"},"7803":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-247","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"Moves the newest past entry to future, restores its before-values, autosaves. Returns false when past is empty or the file is not ready. A no-op undo (entry resolves to the current document) still advances the stack but skips write/revision. Any undo cancels a pending save() checkpoint. Defaults to homeConfig."},"7804":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-248","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"ConfigStore.redo(fileKey)"},"7805":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-249","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"Moves the newest future entry back to past, restores its after-values, autosaves. Returns false when future is empty or the file is not ready. No-op redos advance the stack without write/revision. A new set()/update()/remove() clears future. Defaults to homeConfig."},"7806":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-250","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"ConfigStore.revert(fileKey)"},"7807":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-251","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"Logically while (canUndo) undo(): replays every past before-value in reverse to restore the clean baseline, coalesced into a single document commit (single write, single revision, single documentUpdated). Then wipes past + future. Returns false when not ready, or when past is empty and already clean. Undone-to-clean with redo available wipes without disk IO. Defaults to homeConfig."},"7808":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-252","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"ConfigStore.save(fileKey)"},"7809":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-253","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"True checkpoint. Fails (false) when not ready. Clean + empty history: true no-op, no IO. Clean with leftover history (e.g. undo-to-clean leaves redo): wipes history, true, no IO, no revision. Dirty + write pipeline active: marks checkpoint-when-idle and ensures the newest state is queued; baseline/history reset in onSaved. Dirty + idle + last write failed: forces a rewrite, checkpoint on onSaved. Dirty + idle + disk already matches (normal autosave case): sets baseline + wipes history synchronously, true, no IO."},"7810":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-254","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"How to call"},"7811":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-255","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"What does it do"},"7812":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-256","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"ConfigStore.save(fileKey)"},"7813":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-257","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"True checkpoint (see Undo history). Defaults to homeConfig. Normal set()/update()/remove() already autosave; save() only moves the baseline and wipes history."},"7814":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-258","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"ConfigStore.reload(fileKey)"},"7815":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-259","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"Explicitly reloads one file from disk (controller.forceReload()). Discards unsaved local state for that file (baseline = disk, history wiped). Defaults to homeConfig. Rejected while the write pipeline is active."},"7816":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-260","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"ConfigStore.reloadAll()"},"7817":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-261","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"Reloads every registered file. Skips files currently being written."},"7818":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-262","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"Example"},"7819":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-263","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"Result"},"7820":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-264","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"ConfigStore.save()"},"7821":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-265","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"true checkpoint for homeConfig; false when no controller exists or not ready"},"7822":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-266","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"ConfigStore.save(\"networkConfig\")"},"7823":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-267","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"true checkpoint for networkConfig; false when no controller exists or not ready"},"7824":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-268","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"ConfigStore.reload()"},"7825":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-269","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"true and homeConfig reloaded (local dirty state discarded); false while writing or when no controller exists"},"7826":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-270","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"ConfigStore.reload(\"networkConfig\")"},"7827":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-271","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"true and networkConfig reloaded; false while writing or when no controller exists"},"7828":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-272","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"ConfigStore.reloadAll()"},"7829":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-273","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"true when every file reloaded; false when one or more files were skipped or failed"},"7830":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-274","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"How to call"},"7831":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-275","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"What does it do"},"7832":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-276","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"ConfigStore.registerPath(fileKey, fsPath)"},"7833":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-277","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"Registers one logical file key and creates its document, state, baseline, history, and (via pathKeys) its controller. Same key plus same path is idempotent (true). Rejects empty keys/paths, same key with a different path, and duplicate physical paths."},"7834":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-278","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"ConfigStore.registerPaths(pathTable)"},"7835":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-279","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"Registers multiple files at once. Requires an object. Returns false when one or more entries fail (still registers the ones that succeed)."},"7836":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-280","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"ConfigStore.hasPath(fileKey)"},"7837":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-281","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"Registry lookup. Returns true when the key is registered, false otherwise (including empty keys). Does not fall back to homeConfig."},"7838":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-282","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"ConfigStore.pathFor(fileKey)"},"7839":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-283","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"Returns the resolved physical path for a key. Unknown keys resolve to the homeConfig path (with a one-time warning)."},"7840":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-284","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"ConfigStore.updatePath(fileKey, fsPath)"},"7841":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-285","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"Changes the physical path of an existing non-default key, discards its old document, resets state/history/baseline, resets the controller's directory/write flags, and force-reloads the new file. Rejects homeConfig, unregistered keys, empty paths, active write pipelines / dirty-write state, and duplicate physical paths. Same-path updates are a true no-op."},"7842":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-286","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"ConfigStore.removePath(fileKey)"},"7843":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-287","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"Removes a non-default key plus its document, state, history, baseline, and (via pathKeys) its controller. Leaves the physical file untouched. Rejects homeConfig, unregistered keys, and active write pipelines / dirty-write state."},"7844":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-288","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"Example"},"7845":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-289","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"Result"},"7846":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-290","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"ConfigStore.registerPath(\"networkConfig\", \"~/.config/N0ctOS/network.json\")"},"7847":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-291","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"true and key registered plus controller created; true when already registered with the same path; false on empty key/path, conflicting path, or duplicate physical path"},"7848":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-292","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"ConfigStore.registerPaths({networkConfig: \"~/.config/N0ctOS/network.json\"})"},"7849":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-293","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"true when every entry registered; false when one or more entries failed or the table is not an object"},"7850":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-294","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"ConfigStore.hasPath(\"networkConfig\")"},"7851":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-295","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"true when registered, false otherwise (no fallback)"},"7852":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-296","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"ConfigStore.pathFor(\"networkConfig\")"},"7853":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore-297","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#path-registry","content":"Resolved path, e.g. \"/home/user/.config/N0ctOS/network.json\"; homeConfig path when the key is unknown"},"7854":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell