docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"What does it do"},"8497":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-193","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.get(dataPath, fallbackValue, fileKey)"},"8498":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-194","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"Reads a value at a dotted data path. Returns fallbackValue when missing or when the path is empty. Unknown fileKey warns once, then falls back to homeConfig."},"8499":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-195","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.has(dataPath, fileKey)"},"8500":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-196","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"Checks whether a property exists (sentinel-based, so stored undefined-shaped gaps still report correctly). Unknown fileKey warns once, then falls back to homeConfig."},"8501":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-197","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.documentFor(fileKey)"},"8502":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-198","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"Returns a snapshot clone of the complete document for a file key. Mutating the returned object never affects the store; use set()/update()/remove()/undo()/redo()/revert(). Unknown fileKey warns once, then falls back to homeConfig. Returns {} when no document exists."},"8503":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-199","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.historyAt(fileKey)"},"8504":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-200","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"{past:[...], future:[...], canUndo, canRedo, count, limit, isDirty} for the file. Each entry is {op, dataPath, changeCount, changes:[{path, beforeExists, beforeValue, afterExists, afterValue}]}. future[0] is the next redo. Unknown keys fall back to homeConfig."},"8505":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-201","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.historyFor(fileKey)"},"8506":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-202","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"Alias of historyAt(). Kept for convenience."},"8507":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-203","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"Example"},"8508":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-204","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"Result"},"8509":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-205","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.get(\"notifications.isDnd\", false)"},"8510":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-206","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"Stored value, or false when missing"},"8511":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-207","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.get(\"wifi.enabled\", true, \"networkConfig\")"},"8512":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-208","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"Stored value from networkConfig, or true when missing; homeConfig value when key is unknown"},"8513":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-209","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.has(\"notifications.isDnd\")"},"8514":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-210","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"true when the property exists, false when it does not"},"8515":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-211","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.documentFor(\"networkConfig\")"},"8516":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-212","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"Full document snapshot (read-only: mutate via set()/update()/remove(), never by editing the returned object)"},"8517":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-213","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.historyAt(\"networkConfig\")"},"8518":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-214","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"history detail for networkConfig"},"8519":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-215","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.historyFor(\"networkConfig\")"},"8520":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-216","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"same as historyAt()"},"8521":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-217","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.isReadyFor(\"networkConfig\")"},"8522":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-218","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"true when ready"},"8523":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-219","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.isWritingFor(\"networkConfig\")"},"8524":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-220","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"true while writing"},"8525":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-221","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.isDirtyFor(\"networkConfig\")"},"8526":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-222","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"true when unsaved changes exist"},"8527":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-223","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"ConfigStore.revisionFor(\"networkConfig\")"},"8528":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-224","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#reads","content":"revision number, 0 when no state exists"},"8529":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-225","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"How to call"},"8530":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-226","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"What does it do"},"8531":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-227","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"ConfigStore.set(dataPath, value, fileKey)"},"8532":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-228","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"Creates or updates one value. Missing intermediate objects are created automatically. Autosaves immediately (memory + disk write queued). No-op (true, no write, no revision) when already equal. Rejects empty paths and undefined values. Unknown fileKey warns once, then falls back to homeConfig."},"8533":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-229","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"ConfigStore.update(dataPath, value, fileKey)"},"8534":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-230","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"Deep-merges an object value into a data path, then persists through the normal autosave path. Requires a non-empty path and an object value. Unknown fileKey warns once, then falls back to homeConfig."},"8535":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-231","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"ConfigStore.remove(dataPath, fileKey)"},"8536":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-232","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"Deletes a nested property and autosaves. Returns false and changes nothing when the path does not exist. Unknown fileKey warns once, then falls back to homeConfig."},"8537":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-233","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"Example"},"8538":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-234","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"Result"},"8539":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-235","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"ConfigStore.set(\"notifications.isDnd\", true)"},"8540":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-236","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"true and document changed plus autosave write queued; true with no write/revision when already equal; false on empty path or undefined value"},"8541":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-237","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"ConfigStore.update(\"notifications\", {\"isDnd\": true})"},"8542":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-238","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"true and value deep-merged plus autosave write queued; false when path is empty or value is not an object"},"8543":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-239","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"ConfigStore.remove(\"notifications.isDnd\")"},"8544":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-240","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"true and property deleted plus autosave write queued; false when the path did not exist"},"8545":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-241","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#writes","content":"There are no setAt / updateAt / removeAt / getAt QML variants on the store itself: the fileKey third (or second) parameter already selects the file. The *At naming exists only on the IPC layer (getAt, setJsonAt, updateJsonAt, removeAt, saveAt, reloadAt, isReadyAt, and so on)."},"8546":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-242","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"Model: autosave everything + explicit checkpoint. Every set()/update()/remove()/undo()/redo()/revert() updates memory and immediately queues a disk write. isDirty means \"document differs from the last save()/load baseline\", not \"disk differs\" — after autosave the file already matches memory, but the file stays dirty until save() establishes a new baseline and wipes history."},"8547":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-243","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"Each mutation records one compact forward-delta entry (past), up to historyLimit (100) entries for past + future combined. When over the limit the oldest past entry is discarded first so redo is preserved. A new mutation clears future (kills redo). save() and revert() wipe both stacks."},"8548":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-244","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"How to call"},"8549":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-245","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"What does it do"},"8550":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-246","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"ConfigStore.undo(fileKey)"},"8551":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-247","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"Moves the newest past entry to future, restores its before-values, autosaves. Returns false when past is empty or the file is not ready. A no-op undo (entry resolves to the current document) still advances the stack but skips write/revision. Any undo cancels a pending save() checkpoint. Defaults to homeConfig."},"8552":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-248","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"ConfigStore.redo(fileKey)"},"8553":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-249","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"Moves the newest future entry back to past, restores its after-values, autosaves. Returns false when future is empty or the file is not ready. No-op redos advance the stack without write/revision. A new set()/update()/remove() clears future. Defaults to homeConfig."},"8554":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-250","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"ConfigStore.revert(fileKey)"},"8555":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-251","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"Logically while (canUndo) undo(): replays every past before-value in reverse to restore the clean baseline, coalesced into a single document commit (single write, single revision, single documentUpdated). Then wipes past + future. Returns false when not ready, or when past is empty and already clean. Undone-to-clean with redo available wipes without disk IO. Defaults to homeConfig."},"8556":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-252","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"ConfigStore.save(fileKey)"},"8557":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-253","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#undo-history","content":"True checkpoint. Fails (false) when not ready. Clean + empty history: true no-op, no IO. Clean with leftover history (e.g. undo-to-clean leaves redo): wipes history, true, no IO, no revision. Dirty + write pipeline active: marks checkpoint-when-idle and ensures the newest state is queued; baseline/history reset in onSaved. Dirty + idle + last write failed: forces a rewrite, checkpoint on onSaved. Dirty + idle + disk already matches (normal autosave case): sets baseline + wipes history synchronously, true, no IO."},"8558":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-254","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"How to call"},"8559":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-255","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"What does it do"},"8560":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-256","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"ConfigStore.save(fileKey)"},"8561":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-257","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"True checkpoint (see Undo history). Defaults to homeConfig. Normal set()/update()/remove() already autosave; save() only moves the baseline and wipes history."},"8562":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-258","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"ConfigStore.reload(fileKey)"},"8563":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-259","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"Explicitly reloads one file from disk (controller.forceReload()). Discards unsaved local state for that file (baseline = disk, history wiped). Defaults to homeConfig. Rejected while the write pipeline is active."},"8564":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-260","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"ConfigStore.reloadAll()"},"8565":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-261","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"Reloads every registered file. Skips files currently being written."},"8566":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-262","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"Example"},"8567":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-263","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"Result"},"8568":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-264","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"ConfigStore.save()"},"8569":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-265","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#file-control","content":"true checkpoint for homeConfig; false when no controller exists or 