:"There are two layers:"},"8983":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-679","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#61-overall-architecture","content":"Everyday UI normally interacts only with Config. Store-level consumers interact with ConfigStore directly for controller insight, documentUpdated semantics, debug control, and IPC behavior."},"8984":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-680","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#62-the-file-registry","content":"The store maintains a logical path table:"},"8985":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-681","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#62-the-file-registry","content":"The keys are logical identifiers. The values are resolved physical paths. Consumers therefore operate on:"},"8986":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-682","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#62-the-file-registry","content":"instead of:"},"8987":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-683","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#62-the-file-registry","content":"_paths is the table, _pathKeys is its key list (the Instantiator model), and _registryRevision is bumped on every registry/controller change so reactive reads (pathFor(), documentFor(), state getters) reevaluate."},"8988":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-684","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#63-homeconfig","content":"homeConfig is the default configuration key:"},"8989":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-685","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#63-homeconfig","content":"Its path is based on:"},"8990":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-686","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#63-homeconfig","content":"when available. Otherwise:"},"8991":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-687","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#63-homeconfig","content":"is used. The resulting default path is:"},"8992":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-688","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#63-homeconfig","content":"or:"},"8993":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-689","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#63-homeconfig","content":"homeConfig is always present and cannot be removed or redirected. Unknown file keys resolve to it (with a one-time warning per key)."},"8994":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-690","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#64-key-resolution-fallback-vs-exact","content":"Two different normalizers serve two different API families:"},"8995":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-691","page_id":"section::docs/shell: