figstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#65-documents-states-baselines-history","content":"External watcher changes become op: \"externalReload\" entries with the baseline left in place — which is why an external edit reads as dirty and is undoable."},"9001":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-697","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#66-read-path","content":"Reads never touch the filesystem. They observe the in-memory document, which the controllers keep synchronized."},"9002":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-698","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#67-write-path","content":"Every committed mutation autosaves. documentUpdated(fileKey) fires once per commit. revert() coalesces its full-baseline restore into a single commit (single write, single revision, single signal)."},"9003":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-699","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#68-undo--redo--revert-internals","content":"No-op undo/redo (entry resolves to the current document) still advances the stacks but skips write/revision."},"9004":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-700","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/configstore#69-save--reload-internals","content":"save() is a checkpoint, not a write: normal mutations already persist. reload() is destructive by design (local state discarded, baseline = disk)."},"9005":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstore-701","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/configstor