s are allowed to overlap:"},"14994":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-312","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#one-shot-overlap","content":"A busy preloaded voice is never stolen mid-playback; a fresh temporary voice is created instead. This is why rapid clicking produces overlapping clicks rather than cut-off audio."},"14995":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-313","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#exactly-one-loop-per-sound","content":"Loops enforce a singleton voice:"},"14996":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-314","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#exactly-one-loop-per-sound","content":"Calling loop() twice does not stack two ambient layers."},"14997":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-315","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#voice-lifecycle-mediaplayer--audiooutput--releasetimer","content":"Every voice is:"},"14998":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-316","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#voice-lifecycle-mediaplayer--audiooutput--releasetimer","content":"The volume binding is live:"},"14999":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-317","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#voice-lifecycle-mediaplayer--audiooutput--releasetimer","content":"so changing masterVolume affects already-loaded voices without reconfiguration."},"15000":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-318","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#voice-lifecycle-mediaplayer--audiooutput--releasetimer","content":"Idle voices linger for one second:"},"15001":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-319","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#voice-lifecycle-mediaplayer--audiooutput--releasetimer","content":"Preloaded (keepLoaded) voices skip the timer and stay resident until the definition changes, preload is disabled, or the sound disappears."},"15002":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-320","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#preload-reconciliation","content":"Every Config.revision change (while Config.isReady) runs _reconcile():"},"15003":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-321","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#preload-reconciliation","content":"enabled always wins over preload: a disabled sound is never preloaded, even with preload: true."},"15004":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-322","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#reactive-configuration","content":"profile, isEnabled, and masterVolume are bindings over Config.revision:"},"15005":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-323","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#reactive-configuration","content":"External config edits (file, IPC, another component) propagate without an explicit reload call. _reconcile() also runs on onRevisionChanged so voices track the new definitions."},"15006":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-324","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#change-signals","content":"Imperative consumers (OSDs, debug overlays, logging) use:"},"15007":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-325","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#change-signals","content":"Reactive bindings (profile text, volume sliders, looping indicators) do not need these signals."},"15008":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-326","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#config-integration","content":"The service does not implement its own JSON persistence. All state lives in:"},"15009":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-327","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#config-integration","content":"inside:"},"15010":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-328","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#config-integration","content":"via Config.get() / Config.set() / Config.remove() / Config.has()."},"15011":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-329","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#json-serialization-for-ipc","content":"getStatus() returns a plain object that is JSON.stringify()-ed by IPC. getSFX() / getProfile() results are likewise stringified (\"null\" when missing), so terminal scripts receive valid JSON."},"15012":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-330","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#no-01-clamp-on-master-volume","content":"setMasterVolume() retains the value exactly:"},"15013":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-331","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#no-01-clamp-on-master-volume","content":"Qt's AudioOutput applies its own final playback range. The service intentionally does not cap, mirroring the stored value in getMasterVolume() / masterVolume."},"15014":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-332","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#no-01-clamp-on-master-volume","content":"Non-finite input (NaN, Infinity, non-numeric strings) returns false and stores nothing. Reads of a missing/non-numeric stored value fall back to 1.0."},"15015":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-333","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#one-shots-cannot-be-stopped","content":"There is no stopOneShot():"},"15016":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-334","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#one-shots-cannot-be-stopped","content":"stop() only resolves _findLoopVoice(). A one-shot, once started, plays to completion (or until a profile switch / disable destroys its voice)."},"15017":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-335","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#profile-names-are-trimmed-strings","content":"_cleanProfileName() trims whitespace. Empty-after-trim names are rejected by every profile function. Profile names are case-sensitive and must be valid Config path segments (no dots — a dot would create a nested config path)."},"15018":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-336","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#createprofile-requires-an-object","content":"Arrays, strings, numbers, null, and undefined return false. Existing profiles are never overwritten — use setSFX() with a {name, profile} target or Config.set() to edit an existing profile."},"15019":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-337","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#renameprofile-copies-then-deletes","content":"Rename is not atomic at the config level:"},"15020":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-338","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#renameprofile-copies-then-deletes","content":"Renaming to an existing name, renaming a missing source, or renaming with empty/same names all return false."},"15021":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-339","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#profile-switching-destroys-voices","content":"selectProfile() to a different profile calls _stopAllVoices() before switching. Both one-shots and loops are destroyed, not faded. removeProfile() of the active profile does the same while resetting to \"default\"."},"15022":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-340","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#missing-profile-object-means-enabled","content":"When the active profile has no stored object:"},"15023":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-341","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#missing-profile-object-means-enabled","content":"A profile only disables playback when its stored enabled field is explicitly false. This keeps fresh installs audible before any profile object exists."},"15024":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-342","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#sound-level-enabled-overrides-everything","content":"A sound with enabled: false is never played, looped, or preloaded, regardless of profile enabled or preload flags. configure() and start() both re-check this."},"15025":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-343","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#ipc-json-must-be-valid","content":"setSFX / createProfile IPC parse <json> with JSON.parse() and return false on failure with a [SoundFX] warning. String sound values must therefore be JSON-quoted:"},"15026":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-344","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#no-per-voice-volume-ipc","content":"There is no setVolume <name> <value> IPC. Per-sound volume is config state — write it via setSFX <name>.volume <json-number> and the live AudioOutput.volume binding picks it up."},"15027":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-345","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#51-click-sounds-on-buttons","content":"The most common usage — one line per interaction:"},"15028":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-346","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#51-click-sounds-on-buttons","content":"When the profile is disabled or the sound has no path, play() returns false and the click handling still runs — audio never blocks UI logic."},"15029":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-347","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#52-a-mute--enable-toggle","cont