ndfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#61-overall-architecture","content":"SoundFX should not duplicate functionality already provided by Config or QtMultimedia."},"15061":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-379","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#62-configuration-structure","content":"The service owns the soundfx section of homeConfig."},"15062":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-380","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#62-configuration-structure","content":"The structure is:"},"15063":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-381","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#62-configuration-structure","content":"Field semantics:"},"15064":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-382","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#62-configuration-structure","content":"Everything else (voices, players, timers) is runtime state, not stored configuration."},"15065":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-383","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#63-profile-resolution","content":"_currentProfile() calls _profileName() with no argument, so the active profile is always the stored selection. _currentProfileObject() and _currentProfileEnabled() build on it:"},"15066":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-384","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#63-profile-resolution","content":"_masterVolume() reads soundfx.masterVolume with a defaultMasterVolume (1.0) fallback for missing/non-finite values and deliberately skips clamping."},"15067":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-385","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#64-target-parsing","content":"_parseTarget(obj) produces:"},"15068":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-386","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#64-target-parsing","content":"Object targets read name (or path as a name alias when property is absent), plus optional property and non-blank profile. When the resulting name contains a . and no explicit property was given, _splitTargetPath() splits on the first dot:"},"15069":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-387","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#64-target-parsing","content":"String targets assign the whole string to name first, then split the same way. _soundConfigPath(profile, name, property) then builds:"},"15070":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-388","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#64-target-parsing","content":"getSFX() reads via _deepGet() (dot-splitting, null fallback): first the sound object at target.name, then the nested value at target.property when non-empty. setSFX() writes the same config path via Config.set()."},"15071":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-389","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#64-target-parsing","content":"isSFXEnabled() forces target.property = \"enabled\" after parsing, so:"},"15072":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-390","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#64-target-parsing","content":"both read the sound's enabled flag through getSFX() and coerce with Boolean()."},"15073":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-391","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#65-play-semantics","content":"play() never steals a busy voice: when the retained/preloaded voice is busy, a second temporary voice carries the overlapping one-shot."},"15074":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-392","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#66-loop--stop-semantics","content":"stop() matches by exact soundName through _findLoopVoice(). One-shot voices are invisible to it."},"15075":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-393","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#67-voice-object-model","content":"Each voice is an Item created from voiceComponent:"},"15076":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-394","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#67-voice-object-model","content":"configure() stops old playback, clears source, snapshots the definition (with a 1.0 volume fallback), sets loops (Infinite vs 1), and assigns player.source. When the definition is disabled or pathless it records the definition but leaves the player sourceless — start() will then refuse."},"15077":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-395","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#67-voice-object-model","content":"start() stops the release timer, sets loops, clears stale, marks busy/started, and calls player.play()."},"15078":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-396","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#67-voice-object-model","content":"stopLoop() on a non-loop returns false. Otherwise it clears busy/started, stops the player, emits loopStopped() when it was busy, and restarts the release timer unless keepLoaded."},"15079":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-397","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#67-voice-object-model","content":"Child ids (player, releaseTimer, output) are lexical to the component; external code must use playerObject / releaseTimerObject."},"15080":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-398","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#68-natural-finish-and-error-paths","content":"MediaPlayer.onPlaybackStateChanged handles the natural-finish transition:"},"15081":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-399","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#68-natural-finish-and-error-paths","content":"onErrorOccurred emits playbackError(name, errorString), clears busy/started, and schedules release under the same stale/retention rule."},"15082":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-400","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#68-natural-finish-and-error-paths","content":"The 1-second releaseTimer destroys the voice via _destroyVoice() when it fires while idle. _destroyVoice() refuses busy voices, splices the voice out of voices, and calls voice.destroy()."},"15083":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-401","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#69-preload-and-_reconcile","content":"_reconcile() runs on startup (when ready), on Config.onIsReadyChanged, and on every Config.onRevisionChanged. It has two phases: ensure every desired preload has a retained idle voice, then demote or destroy stale voices (see §4 for the full flow)."},"15084":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-402","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#69-preload-and-_reconcile","content":"Desired preloads are sounds in the active profile with enabled && preload && path !== \"\". A busy voice is never converted into a preload voice mid-playback. Changed definitions reconfigure the retained voice in place."},"15085":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-403","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#69-preload-and-_reconcile","content":"Voices whose sound vanished, was disabled, or lost its path are marked stale: loop voices stop immediately (loopStopped + destroy), idle one-shots are destroyed, and busy one-shots finish before their timer fires."},"15086":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-404","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#69-preload-and-_reconcile","content":"Voices that are still valid but no longer desired (or whose preload flipped to false) get keepLoaded = false and a release-timer restart — the normal one-second lazy lifecycle takes over instead of an immediate destroy."},"15087":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-405","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#69-preload-and-_reconcile","content":"Every reconcile ends with configurationChanged(), including the profile-disabled teardown path."},"15088":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-406","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#610-profile-management-internals","content":"Profile switching and active-profile removal use _stopAllVoices() (destroys every voice, clearing sources), while stopAllLoops() only stops loop voices and leaves one-shots and preloaded voices alone."},"15089":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-407","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#611-master-volume-no-clamp-by-design","content":"The configured value is retained exactly so settings UI round-trips losslessly. The audible range is Qt AudioOutput's concern. Reads (masterVolume, getMasterVolume(), _masterVolume()) return the stored number or 1.0 when missing/non-finite."},"15090":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-408","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#612-ipc-architecture","content":"IPC is a thin external interface over the same service functions:"},"15091":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-409","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#612-ipc-architecture","content":"Value-returning reads that produce objects (getStatus, getSFX, getProfile) return JSON.stringify()-ed strings; missing values stringify to \"null\". Boolean actions return the same bool the QML function returns. setSFX / createProfile JSON.parse() their <json> argument and return false with a warning on invalid JSON. Structured targets are accepted as JSON objects for getSFX / setSFX / isEnabled."},"15092":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-410","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#613-final-architecture-summary","content":"The entire system can be viewed as:"},"15093":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-411","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#613-final-architecture-summary","content":"The core rule is:"},"15094":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-412","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#613-final-architecture-summary","content":"Components request what sound they need; SoundFX.qml decides which profile definition it comes from and which voice plays it; QtMultimedia handles how the audio is decoded and output."},"15095":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","type":"page","content":"SoundFX Service","tags":["docs/shell"],"url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx"},"15096":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-0","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx","content":"SoundFX.qml is N0ctOS's centralized sound-effects service."},"15097":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-1","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","type":"heading","tags":["docs/shell"],"url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#1-what-does-it-do","content":"1. What does it do?"},"15098":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-2","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","type":"heading","tags":["docs/shell"],"url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#2-ui-api","content":"2. UI API"},"15099":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-3","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","type":"heading","tags":["docs/shell"],"url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#core-api","content":"Core API"},"15100":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-4","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundf