ing-a-new-sound","content":"From IPC:"},"15458":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-362","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#56-managing-profiles","content":"Create and select a profile:"},"15459":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-363","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#56-managing-profiles","content":"Rename it (active selection follows):"},"15460":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-364","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#56-managing-profiles","content":"Remove it (\"default\" is protected):"},"15461":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-365","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#56-managing-profiles","content":"Inspect:"},"15462":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-366","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#56-managing-profiles","content":"From IPC:"},"15463":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-367","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#57-reacting-to-playback","content":"Use the signals for debug overlays or OSDs:"},"15464":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-368","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#58-status-panel-and-debugging","content":"Show live state:"},"15465":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-369","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#58-status-panel-and-debugging","content":"Dump the full snapshot:"},"15466":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-370","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#58-status-panel-and-debugging","content":"From IPC:"},"15467":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-371","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#59-terminal-workflow","content":"Check state:"},"15468":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-372","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#59-terminal-workflow","content":"Play and loop:"},"15469":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-373","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#59-terminal-workflow","content":"Edit sounds:"},"15470":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-374","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#59-terminal-workflow","content":"Manage profiles and volume:"},"15471":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-375","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#6-detailed-architecture","content":"This section is for developers working on SoundFX.qml and the services/components that consume it."},"15472":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-376","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#61-overall-architecture","content":"The service is a profile-aware voice pool over QtMultimedia with a Config-backed definition layer:"},"15473":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-377","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#61-overall-architecture","content":"There are effectively three responsibilities:"},"15474":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-378","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#61-overall-architecture","content":"SoundFX should not duplicate functionality already provided by Config or QtMultimedia."},"15475":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-379","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#62-configuration-structure","content":"The service owns the soundfx section of homeConfig."},"15476":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-380","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#62-configuration-structure","content":"The structure is:"},"15477":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-381","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#62-configuration-structure","content":"Field semantics:"},"15478":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-382","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#62-configuration-structure","content":"Everything else (voices, players, timers) is runtime state, not stored configuration."},"15479":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-383","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#63-profile-resolution","content":"_currentProfile() calls _profileName() with no argument, so the active profile is always the stored selection. _currentProfileObject() and _currentProfileEnabled() build on it:"},"15480":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-384","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#63-profile-resolution","content":"_masterVolume() reads soundfx.masterVolume with a defaultMasterVolume (1.0) fallback for missing/non-finite values and deliberately skips clamping."},"15481":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-385","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#64-target-parsing","content":"_parseTarget(obj) produces:"},"15482":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-386","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#64-target-parsing","content":"Object targets read name (or path as a name alias when property is absent), plus optional property and non-blank profile. When the resulting name contains a . and no explicit property was given, _splitTargetPath() splits on the first dot:"},"15483":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-387","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#64-target-parsing","content":"String targets assign the whole string to name first, then split the same way. _soundConfigPath(profile, name, property) then builds:"},"15484":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-388","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#64-target-parsing","content":"getSFX() reads via _deepGet() (dot-splitting, null fallback): first the sound object at target.name, then the nested value at target.property when non-empty. setSFX() writes the same config path via Config.set()."},"15485":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-389","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#64-target-parsing","content":"isSFXEnabled() forces target.property = \"enabled\" after parsing, so:"},"15486":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-390","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#64-target-parsing","content":"both read the sound's enabled flag through getSFX() and coerce with Boolean()."},"15487":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-391","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#65-play-semantics","content":"play() never steals a busy voice: when the retained/preloaded voice is busy, a second temporary voice carries the overlapping one-shot."},"15488":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-392","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#66-loop--stop-semantics","content":"stop() matches by exact soundName through _findLoopVoice(). One-shot voices are invisible to it."},"15489":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-393","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#67-voice-object-model","content":"Each voice is an Item created from voiceComponent:"},"15490":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-394","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#67-voice-object-model","content":"configure() stops old playback, clears source, snapshots the definition (with a 1.0 volume fallback), sets loops (Infinite vs 1), and assigns player.source. When the definition is disabled or pathless it records the definition but leaves the player sourceless — start() will then refuse."},"15491":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-395","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#67-voice-object-model","content":"start() stops the release timer, sets loops, clears stale, marks busy/started, and calls player.play()."},"15492":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-396","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#67-voice-object-model","content":"stopLoop() on a non-loop returns false. Otherwise it clears busy/started, stops the player, emits loopStopped() when it was busy, and restarts the release timer unless keepLoaded."},"15493":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-397","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#67-voice-object-model","content":"Child ids (player, releaseTimer, output) are lexical to the component; external code must use playerObject / releaseTimerObject."},"15494":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-398","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#68-natural-finish-and-error-paths","content":"MediaPlayer.onPlaybackStateChanged handles the natural-finish transition:"},"15495":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-399","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#68-natural-finish-and-error-paths","content":"onErrorOccurred emits playbackError(name, errorString), clears busy/started, and schedules release under the same stale/retention rule."},"15496":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-400","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#68-natural-finish-and-error-paths","content":"The 1-second releaseTimer destroys the voice via _destroyVoice() when it fires while idle. _destroyVoice() refuses busy voices, splices the voice out of voices, and calls voice.destroy()."},"15497":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-401","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#69-preload-and-_reconcile","content":"_reconcile() runs on startup (when ready), on Config.onIsReadyChanged, and on every Config.onRevisionChanged. It has two phases: ensure every desired preload has a retained idle voice, then demote or destroy stale voices (see §4 for the full flow)."},"15498":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-402","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#69-preload-and-_reconcile","content":"Desired preloads are sounds in the active profile with enabled && preload && path !== \"\". A busy voice is never converted into a preload voice mid-playback. Changed definitions reconfigure the retained voice in place."},"15499":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-403","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#69-preload-and-_reconcile","content":"Voices whose sound vanished, was disabled, or lost its path are marked stale: loop voices stop immediately (loopStopped + destroy), idle one-shots are destroyed, and busy one-shots finish before their timer fires."},"15500":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-404","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#69-preload-and-_reconcile","content":"Voices that are still valid but no longer desired (or whose preload flipped to false) get keepLoaded = false and a release-timer restart — the normal one-second lazy lifecycle takes over instead of an immediate destroy."},"15501":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-405","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#69-preload-and-_reconcile","content":"Every reconcile ends with configurationChanged(), including the profile-disabled teardown path."},"15502":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-406","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#610-profile-management-internals","content":"Profile switching and active-profile removal use _stopAllVoices() (destroys every voice, clearing sources), while stopAllLoops() only stops loop voices and leaves one-shots and preloaded voices alone."},"15503":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-407","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#611-master-volume-no-clamp-by-design","content":"The configured value is retained exactly so settings UI round-trips losslessly. The audible range is Qt AudioOutput's concern. Reads (masterVolume, getMasterVolume(), _masterVolume()) return the stored number or 1.0 when missing/non-finite."},"15504":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-408","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#612-ipc-architecture","content":"IPC is a thin external interface over the same service functions:"},"15505":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-409","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#612-ipc-architecture","content":"Value-returning reads that produce objects (getStatus, getSFX, getProfile) return JSON.stringify()-ed strings; missing values stringify to \"null\". Boolean actions return the same bool the QML function returns. setSFX / createProfile JSON.parse() their <json> argument and return false with a warning on invalid JSON. Structured targets are accepted as JSON objects for getSFX / setSFX / isEnabled."},"15506":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-410","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#613-final-architecture-summary","content":"The entire system can be viewed as:"},"15507":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-411","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#613-final-architecture-summary","content":"The core rule is:"},"15508":{"id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx-412","page_id":"section::docs/shell::/docs/shell/services/soundfx","tags":["docs/shell"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/soundfx#613-final-architecture-summary","content":"Components request what sound they need; SoundFX.qml decides which profile definition it comes from and which voice plays it; QtMultimedia handles how the audio is decoded and output."},"15509":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","type":"page","content":"SystemTray Service","tags":["docs"],"u