object stays reachable as adapter._nativeItem for actions only."},"15836":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-326","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#pinned-means-not-hidden-model","content":"There is no separate pinned list in config:"},"15837":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-327","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#pinned-means-not-hidden-model","content":"isPinned is defined as:"},"15838":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-328","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#pinned-means-not-hidden-model","content":"and isHidden is a membership test against _hiddenIds. pin()/show() remove the id; unpin()/hide() add it. togglePin() and toggleHidden() are the same storage with opposite polarity plus a find() existence check."},"15839":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-329","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#hidden-id-persistence","content":"The service owns systemTray.hidden and nothing else in that section:"},"15840":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-330","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#hidden-id-persistence","content":"Unknown keys in systemTray are copied through on write, so other services can share the section without being clobbered."},"15841":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-331","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#hidden-id-persistence","content":"syncFromConfig() runs on startup, on Config.onExternalReload, on Config.on_ConfigRevisionChanged (when ready), and on isReady transitions. It emits configurationChanged() and schedules a model sync only when the normalized list actually changed (JSON comparison)."},"15842":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-332","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#debounced-model-sync-with-a-synchronous-escape-hatch","content":"Native add/remove and config changes never rebuild models inline:"},"15843":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-333","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#debounced-model-sync-with-a-synchronous-escape-hatch","content":"refresh IPC calls _syncModels() directly instead of scheduling. This is the refresh → _syncModels nuance: every other path is coalesced through Qt.callLater, while refresh rebuilds synchronously for tests and debugging."},"15844":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-334","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#debounced-model-sync-with-a-synchronous-escape-hatch","content":"_syncModels() walks the instantiator (objectAt(i)), partitions into pinned/hidden by isHidden, collects attention by isAttention, replaces all four arrays at once, and emits attentionChanged()."},"15845":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-335","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#attention-tracking","content":"Attention is derived, not stored:"},"15846":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-336","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#attention-tracking","content":"_refreshAttention() recomputes from the current _items without rewalking the instantiator and is called on every native onStatusChanged. Full _syncModels() recomputes it as well."},"15847":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-337","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#capability-gated-actions","content":"Every action checks its capability first:"},"15848":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-338","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#capability-gated-actions","content":"Failures warn ([SystemTray] activate failed: etc.) and return false. Native calls are wrapped in try/catch so a misbehaving item cannot break the shell."},"15849":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-339","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#launch-prefers-desktop-entries","content":"launch() tries an exact desktop-entry lookup first:"},"15850":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-340","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#launch-prefers-desktop-entries","content":"When the tray id does not correspond to a desktop entry, launch degrades to a normal activation instead of failing."},"15851":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-341","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#single-menu-backend-states","content":"Exactly one tray menu may be active. The backend cycles:"},"15852":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-342","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#single-menu-backend-states","content":"isMenuOpen is backend !== \"none\", so both pending and custom read as open. closeMenu() clears service state before calling ContextMenu.close() so the context menu's own close notification does not emit a second menuClosed. _clearMenuState() is the self-close path: it clears state without calling close() again."},"15853":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-343","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#single-menu-backend-states","content":"The visible menu content is fully service-owned: native QsMenuEntry trees become ContextMenuObj rows (with checkbox/radio glyphs, separators, and recursive submenus), plus a trailing Hide/Show row for the active item. Developers never provide tray menu content."},"15854":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-344","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#async-dbus-menu-loading","content":"DBus menus arrive over several round trips. Both the root menu and each submenu poll briefly:"},"15855":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-345","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#async-dbus-menu-loading","content":"Slow applications therefore fill in instead of staying empty. Lazily populated submenus that only send children after AboutToShow cannot load through QML (no invokable exposed by Quickshell) and stay empty by platform design."},"15856":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-346","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#reactive-configuration","content":"_hiddenIds follows the config file without polling:"},"15857":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-347","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#reactive-configuration","content":"Adapter isHidden reads _hiddenIds live, so persisting a hide/show immediately re-partitions on the next sync."},"15858":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-348","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#json-serialization-for-ipc","content":"_snapshot() converts a live adapter into plain data (id, title, icon, tooltip parts, status, flags, capabilities, category). It intentionally omits the native object and live bindings so the result is JSON-safe for list / pinned / hidden / attention / get and for external scripts."},"15859":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-349","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#no-hidden-id-validation-against-connected-items","content":"hidden[] may contain ids with no connected item. They are remembered (rememberedIds in the hidden IPC) and take effect if the application appears later. There is no garbage collection of stale ids."},"15860":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-350","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#togglepin--togglehidden-require-a-connected-item","content":"Direct pin() / unpin() / hide() / show() operate on raw ids and always persist. The toggle variants find() first:"},"15861":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-351","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#togglepin--togglehidden-require-a-connected-item","content":"Scripts that manage not-yet-running applications must use the non-toggle forms."},"15862":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-352","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#find-is-an-exact-string-match","content":"There is no substring, case-insensitive, or category search. The id is String(native.id || \"\"), so empty-id natives are invisible to lookup."},"15863":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-353","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#actions-need-the-item-to-be-connected","content":"Every action resolves through find(). A remembered-but-disconnected hidden id cannot be activated, scrolled, launched, or menu-opened — false is returned."},"15864":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-354","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#onlymenu-items-cannot-be-activated","content":"hasActivate is false when the native item reports onlyMenu, even when a native activate function exists. Such items are menu-only by protocol; use openMenu()."},"15865":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-355","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#menus-need-hasmenu","content":"openMenu() rejects items without a native menu:"},"15866":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-356","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#menus-need-hasmenu","content":"The service does not synthesize a fallback menu for menuless icons."},"15867":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-357","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#only-one-menu-at-a-time","content":"openMenu() calls closeMenu() first. Opening a second item's menu closes the first (emitting menuClosed for it) before attempting the new one."},"15868":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-358","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#closemenu-is-void","content":"Unlike the boolean actions, closeMenu() (QML and IPC) returns nothing. Whether a menu was open is observable through menuClosed(id) and isMenuOpen, not a return value."},"15869":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-359","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#scroll-arguments-are-coerced-not-validated","content":"passes Number(delta) and Boolean(horizontal) straight to the native call. Non-numeric deltas become NaN at the native layer; the service does not range-check scroll steps."},"15870":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-360","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#category-mapping-is-lossy","content":"Native categories collapse to four strings:"},"15871":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-361","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#category-mapping-is-lossy","content":"The raw numeric category is not exposed."},"15872":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-362","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#51-a-pinned-tray-row","content":"The standard panel pattern — visible icons only, left click activates, right click opens the menu:"},"15873":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-363","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#51-a-pinned-tray-row","content":"The row never touches native items or hidden-id storage."},"15874":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-364","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#52-a-hidden-items-expander","content":"Show overflow icons on demand:"},"15875":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-365","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#52-a-hidden-items-expander","content":"Hiding from the expander is symmetric:"},"15876":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-366","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#53-attention-indicator","content":"Blink or badge when anything needs attention:"},"15877":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-367","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#53-attention-indicator","content":"For imperative reactions (notifications, sounds):"},"15878":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-368","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#54-pin-and-hide-controls","content":"Per-icon context actions (e.g. inside a tooltip or management view):"},"15879":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-369","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#54-pin-and-hide-controls","content":"Persist directly by id when no adapter is at hand:"},"15880":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-370","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#55-launching-an-application-from-the-tray","content":"Prefer the desktop entry, fall back to activation automatically:"},"15881":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-371","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#55-launching-an-application-from-the-tray","content":"From IPC:"},"15882":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-372","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#55-launching-an-application-from-the-tray","content":"When the tray id matches a desktop entry id, the full application launches; otherwise the click-equivalent activation runs."},"15883":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-373","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#56-reacting-to-tray-changes","content":"Use the signals for dynamic UI or logging:"},"15884":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-374","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#56-reacting-to-tray-changes","content":"_syncModels()-driven bindings (counts, lists) do not need these signals — they update through the array properties."},"15885":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-375","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#57-terminal-workflow","content":"Check state:"},"15886":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-376","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#57-terminal-workflow","content":"List items:"},"15887":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-377","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#57-terminal-workflow","content