["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#62-configuration-structure","content":"The service owns the systemTray section's hidden key in homeConfig."},"15895":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-385","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#62-configuration-structure","content":"The structure is:"},"15896":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-386","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#62-configuration-structure","content":"A real configuration might look like:"},"15897":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-387","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#62-configuration-structure","content":"_hiddenIds is the normalized in-memory copy (stringified, deduplicated, blanks dropped). _configSection is the last-seen full systemTray object so writes preserve unknown keys."},"15898":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-388","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#62-configuration-structure","content":"Everything else (connected items, statuses, menus) is live native state, not stored configuration."},"15899":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-389","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#63-adapter-creation","content":"The Instantiator mirrors the native model one-to-one:"},"15900":{"id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray-390","page_id":"project::docs::/docs/shell/services/systemtray","tags":["docs"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/shell/services/systemtray#63-adapter-creation","content":"Adapters are lightweight Items (invisible, 